# Single-Cylinder Reciprocating Engine Mechanism — Design & Build Plan
**SolidWorks Portfolio Project**

This is a mechanism-only build (no combustion, no valvetrain) sized like a small model/demo engine — chosen so every part is easy to machine-reference, easy to dimension defensibly, and easy to animate. All dimensions below are internally consistent (bore/stroke/rod ratio checked) and are a good *starting point* — treat them as a baseline you can justify in your README, not a spec pulled from a real engine.

**Baseline geometry**
- Bore (cylinder ID) = 40 mm
- Stroke = 45 mm → crank throw (crank radius) = 22.5 mm
- Connecting rod length (center-to-center) = 90 mm → L/R ratio = 90/22.5 = 4.0 (good, avoids excessive piston side-thrust; real engines run 3–4.5)

